  "examples": [
    {
      "coptic": "ⲁⲩⲣⲁⲟⲩⲱ ϧⲉⲛϩⲁⲛⲡⲁⲑⲟⲥ ⲛⲧⲉⲡⲓⲧⲱⲙⲧ ⲛⲉⲙϩⲁⲛϩⲩⲇⲟⲛⲏ ϣⲁⲧⲟⲩⲃⲱⲗ ⲙⲡⲓ**ⲁⲛⲁϣ** ⲉⲃⲟⲗ ⲉⲧⲁⲩⲧⲏⲓϥ .",
      "english": "For they fell into passions of hesitation and pleasures until they broke their oath.",
      "source": "Bohairic Lausiac History - Part 1",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:lausiac.boh_lausiac.amelineau_ed:0",
      "dialect": "bohairic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲛⲧⲉⲣϥⲥⲱⲧⲙ ⲇⲉ ⲉⲛⲁⲓ ⲛϭⲓⲡⲥⲟⲛ ⲙⲙⲟⲛⲁⲭⲟⲥ · ⲁϥⲱⲣⲕ ⲛⲟⲩ**ⲁⲛⲁϣ** ϫⲉⲉⲓϣⲁⲛⲕⲧⲟⲓ ϯⲛⲁϫⲓⲧⲕ ⲛⲙⲙⲁⲓ ⲉⲧⲁⲙⲟⲛⲏ ·",
      "english": "And when the monkish brother had heard these things he took an oath, saying, 'When I return I will take thee with me to my monastery';",
      "source": "The Life of John the Kalybites part 1",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:lives.john_kalybites.budge:1-45",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲉⲧⲁⲩϣⲱⲡⲓ ⲇⲉ ϧⲉⲛⲟⲩⲧⲱⲙⲧ ⲛⲁⲩⲉⲙⲓ ⲁⲛ ⲡⲉ ϫⲉⲟⲩ ⲡⲉ ⲉⲧⲟⲩⲛⲁϫⲟϥ ⲙⲁⲗⲓⲥⲧⲁ ⲛⲁⲩϣⲉⲣϩⲗⲓ ⲛϩⲱⲃ ⲁⲛ ⲡⲉ ⲉⲑⲃⲉⲡⲓ**ⲁⲛⲁϣ** ⲉⲧⲁⲩⲱⲣⲕ ⲙⲙⲟϥ ⲙⲡⲓⲇⲓⲁⲕⲱⲛ",
      "english": "They were amazed, they did not know what to say, but they did nothing because of the oath they had sworn to the deacon.",
      "source": "Life of Isaac of Alexandria - part 1",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:lives.boh_isaac.amelineau_ed:1-19",
      "dialect": "bohairic"
    },
    {
